    anxious:   { title: "Anxious — Day Two",     brief: "The second night is often when anxiety peaks — the body is working hard and the mind catches up. Offer a breathing technique: four counts in, hold for four, four counts out. That's the whole intervention right now." },
    triggered: { title: "Triggered — Day Two",   brief: "Tell them cravings on Day Two can feel stronger than Day One because the novelty is gone and the substance is still talking. Remind them: the craving is memory, not need. It's the brain running its old circuit. Name what they can do in the next five minutes to interrupt it." },
